    <!-- §1 Overview -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="overview">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§1</div>
        <h2>System Overview</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Governor's Desk is the sovereign executive tier of the bearerCORE™ platform. It provides
        the Governor, Deputy Governor, and Monetary Committee with macro-level visibility over all
        active corridors, aggregate daily volumes, halt authority, and the governance proposal queue
        for corridor parameter changes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unlike the Supervisor Desk — which operates on individual trade claims — the Governor's Desk
        operates at the corridor infrastructure level. Issuance is authorised automatically by protocol
        conditions; the Governor manages corridor capacity, daily caps, halt decisions, and multi-sig
        governance proposals that affect the operating envelope of the entire network.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-pane-grid">
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-left">
          <h3>Left Pane — Network Status</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Total daily volume (all corridors)</li>
            <li>Active corridors count</li>
            <li>Aggregate corridor health</li>
            <li>Last console refresh timestamp</li>
            <li>Active intervention alerts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-middle">
          <h3>Middle Pane — Corridor Grid</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Sovereign Dashboard: all corridors</li>
            <li>Per-corridor capacity bar</li>
            <li>Liquidity position per corridor</li>
            <li>Halt/Active status indicator</li>
            <li>Pending governance proposals</li>
            <li>Corridor action controls</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-pane dp-pane-right">
          <h3>Right Pane — Governance Queue</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Open governance proposals</li>
            <li>Cap change proposals (multi-sig)</li>
            <li>Halt proposals</li>
            <li>Vote / approve / reject proposals</li>
            <li>Governance proposal history</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Role Hierarchy</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Access Level</th><th>Authorities</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Governor</strong></td>
            <td>Full sovereign access</td>
            <td>Corridor halt/unhalt, governance proposal creation, cap change proposals, all corridor intervention types</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Deputy Governor</strong></td>
            <td>Delegated executive access</td>
            <td>Corridor halt/unhalt (below threshold), governance proposal voting, corridor monitoring</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Monetary Committee</strong></td>
            <td>Multi-sig participants</td>
            <td>Vote on governance proposals. Cannot initiate halts unilaterally.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info">
        <span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Protocol-driven vs. approval-driven:</strong> CBDC issuance at the individual note level
          is protocol-driven — it proceeds automatically when all five issuance eligibility gates pass.
          The Governor does not approve individual trade claims. The Governor sets the operating envelope
          (corridor caps, halt state) within which the protocol automatically authorises or blocks
          issuance.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §2 Governance Model -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="governance">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§2</div>
        <h2>Governance Model</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Multi-Signature Requirement</h3>
      <p>
        Corridor parameter changes — daily cap adjustments, velocity limit changes, per-transaction
        cap modifications — require multi-signature governance proposals. A single Governor action
        creates a <em>proposal</em>; a second authorised actor (Deputy Governor or Monetary Committee
        member) must vote to approve before the change takes effect.
      </p>
      <p>
        Emergency halt operations are exempt from the multi-sig requirement: a Governor or Deputy
        Governor may halt a corridor immediately with a single action, followed by a mandatory
        post-hoc audit justification entry.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Action Type</th><th>Multi-Sig Required</th><th>Initiator</th><th>Second Signer</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Daily cap increase</td><td>Yes</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>Monetary Committee</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Daily cap decrease</td><td>Yes</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>Monetary Committee</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Velocity limit change</td><td>Yes</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>Monetary Committee</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-transaction cap change</td><td>Yes</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>Monetary Committee</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Emergency corridor halt</td><td>No — post-hoc audit required</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>N/A</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Corridor unhalt</td><td>No — audit entry required</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td><td>N/A</td></tr>
          <tr><td>FX rate proposal</td><td>Yes</td><td>Central Bank operator</td><td>Governor / Deputy Gov</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Four-Eyes Enforcement</h3>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger">
        <span class="dp-ci">⛔</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Proposer cannot self-approve.</strong> The operator who creates a governance proposal
          cannot cast the approving vote. This is enforced server-side on <code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/:id/vote</code>.
          Any attempt to self-approve returns HTTP 403 with error code <code>self_approval_forbidden</code>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §3 Console Specification -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="panes">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Console Pane Specification</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Console Loading Sequence</h3>
      <p>
        On modal open, <code>loadMacroConsole()</code> fires and executes the following API calls
        in parallel:
      </p>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load corridors</h4><p><code>GET /api/v2/corridors?per_page=50</code>. Returns all registered corridors with status, mode, bloc, and asset code.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load liquidity positions</h4><p><code>GET /api/v2/corridors/:id/liquidity_position</code> for each active corridor. Populates per-corridor capacity bars.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load governance proposals</h4><p><code>GET /api/v2/governance/proposals?status=pending</code>. Populates governance proposal queue panel.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Compute network aggregates</h4><p>Network Status Bar calculates: total daily volume (sum of corridor positions), active corridor count, aggregate health (avg headroom %). Sets govNetLastUpdate timestamp.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Network Status Bar (4 KPI tiles)</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>KPI</th><th>Element ID</th><th>Calculation</th><th>Visual</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Total Daily Volume</strong></td><td class="f">govNetVolume</td><td>Sum of domestic_available across all active corridors</td><td>Dark navy tile, large bold number</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Active Corridors</strong></td><td class="f">govNetActiveCorridors</td><td>Count of corridors with status == active</td><td>Dark navy tile, teal number / total count</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Corridor Health</strong></td><td class="f">govNetHealth</td><td>Average headroom % across all active corridors (net_position / daily_cap)</td><td>Dark navy tile, teal % value</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Last Updated</strong></td><td class="f">govNetLastUpdate</td><td>Timestamp of most recent console refresh</td><td>Dark navy tile, monospace timestamp</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Active System Intervention Panel</h3>
      <p>
        <code>id="govInterventionPanel"</code> — shown only when one or more corridors are in a
        non-normal state (halted, frozen, under intervention). Displays a banner per affected corridor
        with status, intervention type, initiating actor, and elapsed time since intervention. Hidden
        when all corridors are in normal operation.
      </p>

      <h3>Sovereign Dashboard — Corridor Grid</h3>
      <p>
        Populated from <code>GET /api/v2/corridors</code> response. Each corridor renders as a
        card with:
      </p>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Corridor code</td><td>corridor.code</td><td>e.g. NGA-GHA</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Source → Target flags</td><td>corridor.source_country, corridor.target_country</td><td>ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 mapped to emoji flags</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Asset code</td><td>corridor.asset_code</td><td>ISO 4217</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bloc tag</td><td>corridor.bloc</td><td>ECOWAS | EAC | SADC | CEMAC | AMU</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Status badge</td><td>corridor.status</td><td>ACTIVE (green) | HALTED (red) | PAUSED (amber) | FROZEN (red-dark)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Capacity bar</td><td>liquidity_position.net_position / daily_cap</td><td>Visual progress bar, colour-coded by utilisation %</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Domestic Available</td><td>liquidity_position.domestic_available</td><td>Active lock total for corridor</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Halt / Unhalt button</td><td>corridor.status</td><td>Red Halt shown when active; Teal Unhalt shown when halted</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §4 Network Status -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="network">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§4</div>
        <h2>Network Health Monitoring</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Corridor Health Thresholds</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Headroom %</th><th>Health Status</th><th>Visual</th><th>Governor Action</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>&gt; 60%</td><td>Healthy</td><td>Teal / green capacity bar</td><td>Monitor only</td></tr>
          <tr><td>30% – 60%</td><td>Adequate</td><td>Amber capacity bar</td><td>Optional rebalancing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10% – 30%</td><td>Low</td><td>Orange capacity bar</td><td>Recommend liquidity injection</td></tr>
          <tr><td>&lt; 10%</td><td>At Risk</td><td>Red capacity bar, intervention alert</td><td>Required action: rebalance or halt</td></tr>
          <tr><td>0% (negative)</td><td>Deficit</td><td>Dark red, govInterventionPanel shown</td><td>Mandatory halt or emergency governance proposal</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Corridor Status Capability Matrix</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>New Locks</th><th>Release Locks</th><th>Issuance</th><th>Claims</th><th>Governance</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="s-active">ACTIVE</span></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Via proposal</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="s-pending">PAUSED</span></td><td>✗</td><td>✓</td><td>✗</td><td>New claims blocked</td><td>Via proposal</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="s-expired">HALTED</span></td><td>✗</td><td>Emergency only</td><td>✗</td><td>All blocked</td><td>Via Governor</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="s-expired">FROZEN</span></td><td>✗</td><td>✗</td><td>✗</td><td>All blocked</td><td>Via governance only</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §5 Corridor Management -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="corridors">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§5</div>
        <h2>Corridor Management Actions</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Halt Corridor</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Governor clicks Halt on corridor card</h4><p>Confirmation dialog: "Halt corridor NGA-GHA? This will block all new locks, claims, and issuance." Mandatory halt reason required (dropdown: 6 options).</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>API call</h4><p><code>POST /api/v2/corridors/:id/halt {reason: "..."}</code>. Server sets corridor.status = "paused" (or "frozen" for full freeze). Returns updated corridor record.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Network update</h4><p>Active Corridors KPI decrements. Corridor card updates to HALTED badge. govInterventionPanel shows intervention alert. All pending issuance operations for this corridor blocked at five-gate governance check.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Audit</h4><p>CorridorHalted event written: corridor_id, governor_id, reason, halted_at. Immutable. Post-hoc justification mandatory within 4 hours.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Unhalt Corridor</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Governor clicks Unhalt</h4><p>Confirmation: "Resume corridor NGA-GHA?" Requires reason entry.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>API call</h4><p><code>POST /api/v2/corridors/:id/unhalt {reason: "..."}</code>. Server sets corridor.status = "active". Returns updated corridor record.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Network update</h4><p>Active Corridors KPI increments. Corridor card updates to ACTIVE badge. Intervention alert cleared. Issuance eligibility governance gate automatically passes again.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Audit</h4><p>CorridorUnhalted event written: corridor_id, governor_id, reason, unhalted_at.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn">
        <span class="dp-ci">⚠</span>
        <div>
          Halting a corridor does not cancel in-flight trade claims. Claims in <code>approved</code>
          state that have not yet settled will have their issuance eligibility governance gate set to
          <code>passed: false</code> on re-evaluation. Settlement proceeds only after corridor is
          restored to active.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §6 Governance Proposals -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="proposals">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§6</div>
        <h2>Governance Proposals</h2>
      </div>

      <p>
        Corridor parameter changes follow a formal proposal lifecycle. Proposals are created via
        <code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals</code>, visible to all Monetary Committee members,
        and require a second-signer vote before taking effect.
      </p>

      <h3>Proposal Data Model</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="f">id</td><td class="t">uuid</td><td>Proposal primary key</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">corridor_id</td><td class="t">uuid FK</td><td>Target corridor</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">proposal_type</td><td class="t">enum</td><td>cap_change | velocity_change | per_tx_cap_change | fx_rate | halt | freeze</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">proposed_by</td><td class="t">string</td><td>Initiating operator identity</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">proposed_value</td><td class="t">decimal / string</td><td>New value being proposed</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">current_value</td><td class="t">decimal / string</td><td>Value at time of proposal (snapshot)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">justification</td><td class="t">text</td><td>Mandatory rationale from proposer</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">status</td><td class="t">enum</td><td>pending | approved | rejected | recalled</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">votes</td><td class="t">array</td><td>List of {voter, decision, voted_at} records</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">effective_at</td><td class="t">timestamp</td><td>When approved change takes effect (immediate or scheduled)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="f">created_at</td><td class="t">timestamp</td><td>Proposal creation time (UTC)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Proposal Lifecycle</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Create proposal</h4><p><code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals {corridor_id, proposal_type, proposed_value, justification}</code>. Status → pending. ProposalCreated event written.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Notification</h4><p>All Monetary Committee members notified of new pending proposal. Proposal appears in governance queue on Governor's Desk for all eligible voters.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Vote</h4><p><code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/:id/vote {decision: "approve" | "reject"}</code>. Four-Eyes: proposer cannot vote. Required voter count: 1 additional approver for standard changes; 2 for freeze proposals.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Approval threshold reached</h4><p>Server detects sufficient approvals. Status → approved. Corridor parameter updated immediately (or at effective_at for scheduled changes). ProposalApproved event written.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Recall option</h4><p>Proposer may recall a pending proposal before vote threshold is reached via <code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/:id/recall</code>. Cannot recall once approved.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Proposal Status States</h3>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px;">
        <span class="s-pending">PENDING</span>
        <span class="s-active">APPROVED</span>
        <span class="s-expired">REJECTED</span>
        <span class="s-released">RECALLED</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §7 Action Buttons -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="buttons">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§7</div>
        <h2>Action Button Specification</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Refresh Console</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Header Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Label</div><div>↻ Refresh</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Action</div><div><code>loadMacroConsole()</code> — re-fetches corridors, positions, and proposals</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Cooldown</div><div>Button disables for 3s after click to prevent rapid-fire API calls</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Visual</div><div>Teal outline button in console header. Spinner shown during load.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Halt Corridor</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Emergency Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Visible</div><div>On each active corridor card, shown only when corridor.status == active</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Confirmation</div><div>Two-step confirmation dialog. Mandatory halt reason (dropdown). Cannot proceed without reason.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/corridors/:id/halt {reason}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>corridor.status → paused. All new locks and issuance blocked. Governance gate fails for all pending claims.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Audit</div><div>CorridorHalted event written. Post-hoc justification required within 4h.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Auth</div><div>Governor or Deputy Governor role required. Standard supervisor role cannot halt corridors.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Unhalt Corridor</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Recovery Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Visible</div><div>On each halted corridor card, when corridor.status == paused</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/corridors/:id/unhalt {reason}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>corridor.status → active. Issuance eligibility governance gate restored. Pending claims re-eligible.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Audit</div><div>CorridorUnhalted event written with restoration reason.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Create Governance Proposal</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Governance Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Inputs</div><div>Corridor, proposal_type, proposed_value, justification (mandatory)</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>Proposal created in pending state. Monetary Committee notified. Proposer cannot self-vote.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Success</div><div>Proposal appears in governance queue panel. ProposalCreated event written.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Vote on Proposal</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Governance Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Options</div><div>Approve | Reject</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/:id/vote {decision}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Four-Eyes</div><div>Server rejects self-vote with HTTP 403 self_approval_forbidden</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>Vote recorded. If approval threshold reached: parameter updated, corridor notified, ProposalApproved event written.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Recall Proposal</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Governance Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Available</div><div>Only for proposer, only when status == pending</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/:id/recall</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>Status → recalled. Parameter unchanged. ProposalRecalled event written.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §8 Security -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="security">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§8</div>
        <h2>Security &amp; Access Controls</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Implementation</th><th>Enforcement Point</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Role-Based Access</strong></td><td>Governor Desk accessible only to Governor, Deputy Governor, Monetary Committee roles</td><td>Session authentication + RBAC middleware</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Four-Eyes Enforcement</strong></td><td>Proposer ≠ approver on all governance proposals</td><td>Server-side in governance proposals controller</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Halt Authority</strong></td><td>Corridor halt/unhalt restricted to Governor and Deputy Governor roles</td><td>Role check in corridor controller before action</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Audit Immutability</strong></td><td>All governance actions write append-only audit records with actor identity, action, timestamp</td><td>After_action audit writer service</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Session Continuity</strong></td><td>Central bank session required (require_central_bank_access filter on DocsController and all API routes)</td><td>before_action filter on all protected controllers</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Post-Hoc Justification</strong></td><td>Emergency halt requires audit justification entry within 4 hours</td><td>Governance compliance monitoring service</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>No Governor Self-Halt</strong></td><td>A Governor who created a corridor cannot be the sole authority to permanently freeze it — requires Monetary Committee vote</td><td>Governance proposal controller</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger">
        <span class="dp-ci">⛔</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Sovereign deployment segmentation:</strong> The Governor's Desk is deployed on the
          central bank's internal network segment. It is not accessible from the commercial bank
          operator network or public internet. All access is routed through the central bank's zero-trust
          gateway with mandatory MFA.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §9 End-to-End Flow -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="flow">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§9</div>
        <h2>End-to-End Governance Workflow</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Complete walkthrough: Governor responds to low-liquidity alert on NGA→GHA corridor and proposes a daily cap increase.</p>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Open Governor's Desk</h4><p>Governor navigates to sandbox dashboard. Clicks "Governor's Desk". Modal opens. <code>loadMacroConsole()</code> fires. 4 KPI tiles populate. Sovereign Dashboard grid shows all corridors.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Identify low-liquidity corridor</h4><p>Network Status Bar shows Corridor Health at 18% (red). Sovereign Dashboard: NGA-GHA capacity bar at 8% — At Risk. govInterventionPanel shows "NGA-GHA: Liquidity At Risk — 8% headroom remaining".</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Create cap change proposal</h4><p>Governor clicks "Propose Cap Change" on NGA-GHA card. Dialog: Type=cap_change, Proposed Value: 5,000,000 GHS (current: 2,500,000 GHS), Justification: "Q2 seasonal trade volume increase. 90-day review cycle." <code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals</code>.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Proposal enters queue</h4><p>Status → pending. GOV-2026051903 created. Monetary Committee members notified. Proposal appears in governance queue panel. Governor cannot vote on own proposal.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Deputy Governor votes</h4><p>Deputy Governor opens Governor's Desk. Reviews proposal: current 2.5M → proposed 5M GHS, justification noted. Clicks Approve. <code>POST /api/v2/governance/proposals/GOV-2026051903/vote {decision: "approve"}</code>.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Proposal approved</h4><p>Approval threshold reached (1 additional approver sufficient for cap changes). corridor.daily_cap updated to 5,000,000 GHS. ProposalApproved event written. Governance queue panel refreshes — proposal shows APPROVED.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Network updates</h4><p>Console refreshes. NGA-GHA capacity bar recalculates against new daily_cap. Headroom increases from 8% to 54%. Intervention alert cleared. Active claims in pending_review queue may now pass corridor_limits gate.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Audit finalised</h4><p>Full governance chain immutably recorded: proposal creation (Governor identity, timestamp), vote (Deputy Governor identity, timestamp), parameter update (effective_at, old value, new value). Regulatory audit trail complete.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-ok">
        <span class="dp-ci">✓</span>
        <div>End state: NGA-GHA daily cap raised to 5,000,000 GHS via Four-Eyes governance. Full audit chain recorded: proposer, voter, timestamps, old/new values. Corridor health restored. Pending claims unblocked at corridor_limits gate.</div>
      </div>

      <h3>Emergency Halt Flow</h3>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Governor detects anomaly</h4><p>Rapid velocity spike on KES-GHS corridor. Potential settlement integrity risk. Governor initiates halt immediately.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Halt action</h4><p>Two-step dialog. Reason: "Velocity anomaly — investigating potential settlement integrity breach." <code>POST /api/v2/corridors/:id/halt</code>. No multi-sig required for emergency halt.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Immediate effect</h4><p>corridor.status → paused. All new locks, claims, and issuance blocked immediately. Governance gate fails for all pending claims. govInterventionPanel shows active intervention alert.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Investigation &amp; audit</h4><p>Governor investigates via Corridor Ops desk. Within 4 hours: audit justification entry completed. Compliance team notified.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Corridor restored or frozen</h4><p>If investigation clears: <code>POST /corridors/:id/unhalt</code>. If breach confirmed: governance proposal to freeze corridor pending Monetary Committee vote.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

